body:
`kalide render [slide] [-o dir] [--full|--fragment]` writes a deck's rendered slide HTML without serving it (no server, no port, no network; single-binary). With a slide argument it writes the selected slide's HTML to stdout; without a slide argument it writes one file per slide into the directory named by `-o dir`, each file named for its slide's filename stem — `<number>[letter]-<label>.html` (e.g. `3-team.html` for `slides/3-team.md`, `3a-detail.html` for `slides/3a-detail.md`) — in deck order; the no-slide form requires `-o`, and omitting it is a usage error. A slide argument selects a slide by its position label (deck.Slide.PositionLabel: `<number>` for a horizontal slide, `<number><letter>` for a vertical one, e.g. `3` or `3a`, slide-position) or by its deck-unique label (the filename's `<label>`, unique-slide-labels); a position-label match takes precedence over a label match, and an argument matching no slide is an error with a closest-match suggestion. `--full` (the default) writes a complete standalone page — the same page shell, head, embedded assets and theme stylesheet the server serves (pdf-via-print) — whose reveal.js container holds that slide; `--fragment` writes only the slide's `<section>` markup, exactly the fragment the deck page embeds. The two flags are mutually exclusive: giving both is a usage error (exit 2). Output is deterministic — the same deck renders byte-identical HTML across runs, in stable deck order with the slide's label as its anchor id — so the output diffs cleanly in CI and feeds before/after HTML diffs and screenshot tooling. A validation error exits 1 with the error-reporting format (error-reporting); a usage error exits 2.

AC:
- `kalide render 3` (position label) and `kalide render team` (deck label) each print the selected slide's HTML to stdout;
- `kalide render --fragment 3` prints only that slide's `<section>` markup;
- `kalide render -o out` writes one `<number>[letter]-<label>.html` file per slide into `out`, in deck order;
- `kalide render` with no slide argument and no `-o` is a usage error, exit 2;
- `kalide render --full --fragment 3` is a usage error, exit 2;
- on a broken deck `kalide render` exits 1 with the error-reporting format (error-reporting);
- two runs over the same deck produce byte-identical output.
